Please enhance the existing voting UI without changing the current voting business logic, API contracts, database schema, permissions, or role behaviour.

Current behaviour already works:
- Super Admin can vote.
- Normal team users can vote.
- Voting works for all items, including non-P1 items.
- Upvote/downvote counts and selected state already exist.

Implement only these two UI enhancements:

1. Combined voting control in the items table

Replace the currently separated thumbs-up, count, and thumbs-down elements with one compact combined voting control inside the existing “Votes” column.

Expected design:

[ 👍  2  |  👎  0 ]

Requirements:
- Place upvote and downvote inside one rounded container.
- Show the upvote count next to the thumbs-up icon.
- Show the downvote count next to the thumbs-down icon.
- Add a subtle divider between both actions.
- The user’s selected vote must have a clearly filled/highlighted state.
- The unselected action should remain outlined or neutral.
- Clicking the already-selected action should remove the vote if this behaviour is already supported.
- Switching from upvote to downvote, or vice versa, must continue using the existing voting logic.
- Update the count immediately after voting.
- Show a small loading/disabled state while the vote request is processing to prevent repeated clicks.
- Add tooltips:
  - “Upvote this item”
  - “Downvote this item”
  - “Remove your upvote/downvote” when already selected.
- Keep the control compact so it fits properly inside the table row.
- Ensure it is keyboard accessible and add appropriate aria-label attributes.
- Do not restrict this UI to P1 items. It must appear for every item where the logged-in user has voting permission.
- Preserve existing permission checks for normal users, team members and Super Admin.

Suggested reusable component:

<VotingControl
  itemId={item.id}
  upvoteCount={item.upvoteCount}
  downvoteCount={item.downvoteCount}
  currentUserVote={item.currentUserVote}
  canVote={canVote}
  onVote={handleVote}
/>

Create a reusable VotingControl component instead of duplicating the voting UI.

2. Voting information on the item-detail page

Add a dedicated “Voting” section/card on the individual item-detail page.

Suggested UI:

Voting
Team members can vote on this item.

[ 👍 Upvote  12 ]   [ 👎 Downvote  2 ]

Your vote: Upvote

Requirements:
- Place the Voting section in a logical visible location on the item-detail page, preferably near the main item information or contributors section.
- Reuse the same VotingControl component created for the table.
- Show:
  - Total upvotes
  - Total downvotes
  - Logged-in user’s current vote
- Clearly highlight the logged-in user’s selected option.
- If the user has not voted, either show “You have not voted yet” or omit the current-vote label.
- Show instant count updates after voting without requiring page refresh.
- Display a loading state during the vote API request.
- If voting fails, restore the previous count/state and show an existing toast/error message.
- If the user does not have permission to vote, display the counts in read-only mode and show:
  “Only eligible team members can vote on this item.”
- Do not create a new API if existing voting APIs and handlers are already available.
- Do not modify backend permission rules.
- Do not change existing vote records, database tables or API response formats unless absolutely required for rendering.
- Maintain the existing application design system, spacing, typography, colours, dark mode and responsive behaviour.

Implementation approach:
1. Inspect the existing table voting implementation and identify its vote handler, API call and state.
2. Extract the current voting behaviour into a reusable VotingControl component.
3. Replace the existing table voting elements with the combined control.
4. Import and reuse the same component on the item-detail page.
5. Keep one shared voting state update pattern so table and detail views behave consistently.
6. Run linting and TypeScript checks.
7. Test with both Super Admin and normal user accounts.

Acceptance criteria:
- A single combined voting control appears in the Votes column.
- Upvote and downvote counts are both clearly visible.
- The selected vote is visually obvious.
- Voting continues to work for P1, P2, P3, P4 and P5 items.
- The item-detail page contains a dedicated Voting section.
- Table and detail page use the same reusable component.
- Counts update immediately.
- Refreshing the page preserves the vote.
- Existing Super Admin and normal-user voting permissions continue working.
- No existing item-list, filtering, sorting or voting functionality is broken.

Before editing, identify and briefly list the files/components that currently handle:
- The OOO items table
